# Project Instructions

Project:
Financial Data Maintenance & Collection Management System

Technology:
- Java 17
- Spring Boot 3.x
- Spring Data JPA
- SQL Server / Azure SQL
- Angular
- Angular Material
- Reactive Forms
- REST APIs
- Azure Blob Storage

Architecture:
Angular
   ↓
REST API
   ↓
Spring Boot Controller
   ↓
Service / Business Logic
   ↓
Repository
   ↓
SQL Server / Azure SQL

Rules:
1. Financial calculations must be performed in the backend.
2. Do not calculate financial values only in Angular.
3. Do not hard-code interest rates.
4. Business configuration must be configurable.
5. Never delete financial transactions without audit tracking.
6. Maintain createdBy, createdDate, updatedBy, updatedDate.
7. Use proper database transactions for financial operations.
8. Follow existing project architecture where possible.
9. Do not unnecessarily rewrite existing functionality.
10. Reuse existing customer/user/document functionality when appropriate.
11. Validate all financial calculations.
12. Do not expose sensitive customer identification information.
13. Follow existing naming conventions.
14. Before making large changes, explain the proposed changes.
15. Do not modify unrelated files.